-- #467: the farms laid by a station packing rule that's monotone.
--
-- The rural plan asks `station_room::takes(corners, 12)` of every farm it
-- lays. The rule now also tries rows of stations along each side of the lot
-- (`station_room::staggered`), so a farm takes 12 a little smaller, and the
-- lanes hold 911 farms for 900. The farms whose shape changed are released
-- by `20270106_001_packing_rows.sql`; the rural ring's planned nodes draw
-- from different ground, so every one of them moves, as at #347. Nothing
-- outside the rural ring moves. So this deletes the rows the plan no longer
-- has, by id, and inserts the new ones. Nothing a player owns is a node; a
-- node half gathered starts over.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_node_replan`, and
-- `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks the plan still matches.
--
-- deleted 3657 and inserted 3656, all in the rural ring:
--   fallen_branches: 1143 and 1143
--   iron_vein: 152 and 152
--   rock_outcrop: 457 and 457
--   tree: 1905 and 1904

